name: connlog-agent
version: "@VERSION@"
origin: net-mgmt/connlog-agent
comment: "ConnLog monitoring agent: the host's health and, where allowed, its network"
desc: <<EOD
The ConnLog agent for FreeBSD, OPNsense and pfSense. It reports this host's
health to ConnLog and, where its settings allow, what the host knows about
its network: its interfaces, VLANs, ARP and NDP tables and its gateway, and
sweeps of its own subnets. Settings: /usr/local/etc/connlog/agent.conf.
EOD
maintainer: "support@connlog.com"
www: "https://connlog.com"
prefix: /usr/local
# Any FreeBSD on amd64: the binary needs only the base system's libc, whose
# symbols are versioned, so one build runs on OPNsense's 14 and pfSense's 15.
abi: "FreeBSD:*:amd64"
licenselogic: single
licenses: [MIT]
categories: [net-mgmt]
